component Profile {
    goal {
        Stores editable profile information for a signed-in user.

        Keeps profile presentation details separate from authentication identity and
        session rules.
    }

    interface {
        A *UserProfile* has a user identifier, display name, and optional
        profile-picture URL.

        Its *public profile summary* contains the same fields.

        A signed-in user can retrieve their profile and public profile summary by
        user identifier.

        The owning user can update the display name, profile-picture URL, or both.
        An omitted field remains unchanged.

        A successful update returns the updated UserProfile.

        Booking and room views can request the public profile summary for display.
    }

    state {
        profile can be incomplete or complete

        profile belongs to exactly one UserId

        profilePictureUrl can be absent or present
    }

    logic {
        A new user starts with an incomplete profile.

        The owning user can update displayName and profilePictureUrl.

        Booking and room views read profile summary for display only.

        Authentication does not depend on profile completeness.
    }

    constraints {
        Profile owns non-authentication profile fields.

        Auth owns credentials, sessions, roles, and permission checks.

        Other modules should use Profile for display information instead of reading
        Auth private user details.
    }

    cases {
        A renter updates their display name.

        A room owner sets a profilePictureUrl.

        A signed-in user can book a room even when their profile is incomplete.
    }
}
